1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:00,704
Hi!

2
00:00:00,704 --> 00:00:02,673
Meet Qb and Qbo, my two cats.

3
00:00:02,673 --> 00:00:06,475
They look so alike that my camera can't tell them apart.

4
00:00:06,795 --> 00:00:07,997
I'm at work all day.

5
00:00:07,997 --> 00:00:09,199
I just want to know:

6
00:00:09,199 --> 00:00:10,761
did they eat, sleep, play?

7
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:13,345
Cats hide illness, so small changes matter.

8
00:00:13,995 --> 00:00:15,412
But here's the catch:

9
00:00:15,412 --> 00:00:19,193
last week, my camera decided this exercise ball was Qbo.

10
00:00:19,193 --> 00:00:20,745
For twenty-six minutes!

11
00:00:21,065 --> 00:00:23,321
Why not send every frame to a big AI?

12
00:00:23,321 --> 00:00:23,869
We tried:

13
00:00:23,869 --> 00:00:28,990
eight minutes of video took an hour and twenty-five dollars, and still missed a cat.

14
00:00:30,810 --> 00:00:32,456
A bigger model on the Pi?

15
00:00:32,456 --> 00:00:35,681
It only runs YOLO nano, at three frames a second:

16
00:00:35,681 --> 00:00:37,985
almost free, but it makes mistakes.

17
00:00:38,635 --> 00:00:40,805
A bigger detector is out of scope.

18
00:00:40,805 --> 00:00:44,186
We keep the small model, and make it smarter with AI.

19
00:00:44,186 --> 00:00:45,335
So, we built both.

20
00:00:45,655 --> 00:00:48,423
This is Agentic Realtime Computer Vision:

21
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:52,880
the AI gives the camera a brain, and the camera gives the AI eyes.

22
00:00:54,530 --> 00:00:55,776
Here's how it works.

23
00:00:55,776 --> 00:00:57,458
The Pi watches every frame.

24
00:00:57,458 --> 00:01:02,505
When it's unsure, our bridge asks Meta's Muse Spark, and remembers what's normal.

25
00:01:05,155 --> 00:01:06,394
And doubts are rare:

26
00:01:06,394 --> 00:01:07,880
twelve in eight minutes.

27
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:12,072
Each doubt has a name.

28
00:01:12,072 --> 00:01:13,943
There are fifteen kinds, like:

29
00:01:13,943 --> 00:01:16,375
I relabeled this cat by distance alone.

30
00:01:16,695 --> 00:01:21,420
It becomes a plain-English question, with evidence and a strict answer format.

31
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:27,086
Then the agent pulls the frames it needs, zooms into each cat, and answers with a

32
00:01:27,086 --> 00:01:27,520
reason.

33
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:29,669
Related doubts share a call:

34
00:01:29,669 --> 00:01:31,890
twelve questions, just five calls.

35
00:01:32,210 --> 00:01:36,285
Every verdict rewrites the record, and every change is traceable.

36
00:01:36,935 --> 00:01:38,241
Then there's memory.

37
00:01:38,241 --> 00:01:40,722
Not boxes and timestamps, but a diary:

38
00:01:40,722 --> 00:01:44,835
Qb slept in the green bed, from four thirty-four to four forty.

39
00:01:45,155 --> 00:01:49,505
Over weeks, it learns what normal looks like, for each cat, in each spot.

40
00:01:51,655 --> 00:01:52,763
So, does it work?

41
00:01:52,763 --> 00:01:55,369
The tracker called the sleeping cat Qbo.

42
00:01:55,369 --> 00:01:58,237
The agent saw cool white fur and white paws:

43
00:01:58,237 --> 00:01:58,888
that's Qb.

44
00:01:58,888 --> 00:01:59,605
Overturned!

45
00:01:59,925 --> 00:02:03,247
Here, the tracker swapped two cats walking close together.

46
00:02:03,247 --> 00:02:06,225
The agent checked both, and swapped them right back.

47
00:02:06,545 --> 00:02:11,626
When the detector itself is wrong, the cat gets relabeled, and that ball becomes a

48
00:02:11,626 --> 00:02:12,370
known decoy.

49
00:02:12,690 --> 00:02:16,107
Put together, the same eight minutes tell the true story:

50
00:02:16,107 --> 00:02:19,165
Qb slept the whole time, and Qbo walked in and out.

51
00:02:21,485 --> 00:02:22,235
The numbers?

52
00:02:22,235 --> 00:02:27,110
One percent of frames call the AI, false alarms drop ninety-three percent, and

53
00:02:27,110 --> 00:02:30,985
ninety-nine percent of what the camera saw gets the right cat.

54
00:02:30,985 --> 00:02:32,610
All for thirty-nine cents!

55
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:37,144
And cats are just the start:

56
00:02:37,144 --> 00:02:40,710
lab mice, tiny drones, cars in fog, production lines.

57
00:02:40,710 --> 00:02:44,410
Any small model watching for rare moments has this gap.

58
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:46,039
Next:

59
00:02:46,039 --> 00:02:50,853
run Muse Glimmer locally, give your own agent these eyes, and let its verdicts

60
00:02:50,853 --> 00:02:51,655
teach the Pi.

61
00:02:51,975 --> 00:02:54,096
Agentic Realtime Computer Vision.

62
00:02:54,096 --> 00:02:56,539
Built this week, on Meta's Muse Spark.

63
00:02:56,539 --> 00:02:57,825
Thanks for watching!

